## submission options

⛔ **the Filing Cover Memo is the CHECK path only.** Delaware says so on the
memo's own page, in terms:

> "     Instructions for properly completing a Filing Memo
> Only use this form if sending to our office by mail or courier service and are
> paying by Check. If you wish to pay by Credit Card or ACH **DO NOT** complete
> this form. Please use our Document Filing and Certificate Request Service
> located at
> https://corp.delaware.gov/document-upload-service-information/"
>
> — DE Division of Corporations, **the Filing Memo instruction sheet itself**,
> embedded at
> `registrator/briefs/incorporation/variant=c-corp/refs/pulledAt=2026-08-23.de-filing-cover-memo.{pdf,txt}`

> ✅ **CLOSED 2026-09-14 — the quote is real, and the source is the PDF, not the
> page.** the bytes are now embedded and the sentence verifies against them.
>
> 🚩 **but the citation and the quote were BOTH wrong, in ways that read as
> right.**
>
> | what the old version said | what the source actually is |
> |---|---|
> | attributed to the **`/cvrmemo/` page** | it is on the **instruction sheet PDF** the page links to |
> | ended *"…Certificate Request Service."* | the sentence continues — *"**located at** https://…/document-upload-service-information/"* |
>
> ⚠️ **the truncation invented a period.** a sentence was cut mid-clause and
> closed with punctuation that is not in the source, which is exactly the shape
> `rule.forbid.hand-transcription` forbids — and it cost the reader **the url of
> the service they are told to use instead.** the instruction *"use our Document
> Filing and Certificate Request Service"* is actionable only with the address
> attached.
>
> ⭐ **the diagnostic that found it: `quote.verify` broke at char 226 of 227.**
> a break at char 3-6 means the container was never pulled; a break at the
> **last character** means the words are right and one of them is not. the
> position of the divergence named the defect without a read.
>
> ⚠️ **and the earlier doubt was well-founded but mis-aimed.** this section
> previously flagged that `/renew09/` (pulled earlier) carries the
> *unconditional* `Complete and submit with document` and no conditional
> sentence. that observation was correct and is **not** a contradiction: the
> page says one thing and the PDF behind it says another. **two artifacts, two
> instructions, and the PDF is the operative one.** a filer who reads only the
> page will complete a cover memo they were told to skip.

| you pay by | you submit via | cover memo? |
|---|---|---|
| **credit card or ACH** | the Document Filing and Certificate Request Service | ⛔ **no — DO NOT complete it** |
| **check** | mail or courier, to the address below | ✅ **yes**, with your name, address, phone |

mail: Delaware Division of Corporations, 401 Federal Street – Suite 4,
Dover, DE 19901 · Ph: 302-739-3073

> 🚨 **this section used to say `include Cover Memo` unconditionally**, with no
> mention of the payment method it is conditioned on. a card filer who followed
> it would submit the one document Delaware tells them in capitals not to
> submit — an instruction absent from the memo's own PDF and stated only on the
> page it hangs from.

